  "notes": "USAGE:\nSense 1 is very common in elementary school contexts, where {工作|こうさく} refers to arts-and-crafts activities. The school subject is called {図画|ずが}{工作|こうさく} (art and crafts), often abbreviated to {図工|ずこう}. Sense 2 has a negative connotation, implying covert or underhanded activity.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {工作|こうさく}を{作|つく}る: to make a craft\n- {夏休|なつやす}みの{工作|こうさく}: summer vacation craft project\n- {政治|せいじ}{工作|こうさく}: political maneuvering\n- {選挙|せんきょ}{工作|こうさく}: election manipulation\n- {裏|うら}{工作|こうさく}: behind-the-scenes scheming\n- スパイ{工作|こうさく}: espionage activities",
